step Cry of the Thunderhawk
  tip Thunderhawk Cloudscrapers circle over the same plains south of the camp.
  collect 5164 quest 913.1

step Field of Giants
  tip South of Camp Taurajo, the Silithid Mounds dot the Field of Giants; the eggs lie in them, and Silithid Swarmers come out to defend them.
  tip Careful: Silithid Swarmers in the area release many tiny adds that interrupt spells; damage shields such as Thorns kill them in one hit.
  collect 5058 quest 868.1

step Brine
  only Shaman
  zone The Barrens
  tip Brine's hut stands on the ridge above the quilboar watering hole, south of Camp Taurajo: fill the Empty Brown Waterskin at the watering hole below it.
  turnin 1530                         -- Brine
  accept 1535
  collect 7769 quest 1535.1 @44.3,76.8 -- Fill the Empty Brown Waterskin at the quilboar watering hole
  turnin 1535
  accept 1536                         -- Keep it: the Spring Well is beside Tarren Mill, on the Hillsbrad guide

step Twitching Antennae
  zone The Barrens
  only Warrior
  tip The antennae vanish fifteen minutes after they drop: kill the Silithid Swarmers and Creepers at the Field of Giants' mounds, just south of Jorn's thunderhawks, until you have five, then take them straight to Ruga Ragetotem in Camp Taurajo.
  collect 7119 quest 1824.1           -- Twitching Antennae from the silithid
  tip Careful: Silithid Swarmers (level 21-22) cast Silithid Swarm both in and out of combat, which brings several small adds. Silithid Creepers (level 20-21) periodically cast Silithid Creeper Egg in combat, which spawns extra adds.

step Camp Taurajo
  zone The Barrens
  tip Back north into Camp Taurajo on the way to the Crossroads: Jorn takes the thunderhawk wings. Warriors: Ruga Ragetotem first, before the antennae fade.
  turnin 1824 only Warrior            -- Ruga Ragetotem, inside
  accept 1825 only Warrior
  turnin 913                          -- Jorn Skyseer

